  "result": "I made three changes for the three problems. I haven't run the test suite or a type-check.\n\n- **Switching off now sticks:** `updateEndpoint` in `repositories/webhook-repository.ts` dropped `enabled: false` because it only wrote the field when the value was truthy. It now writes it whenever the value is provided, so switching off and back on both save. New events are already skipped for switched-off endpoints in `enqueueForOrg`, so nothing new is queued once the switch-off is saved.\n- **Queued deliveries for switched-off endpoints fail:** `jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts` now marks a delivery failed with \"endpoint is switched off\" when its endpoint is off, and counts it as failed. A missing endpoint was already handled that way. Deliveries for endpoints that are on go out as before.\n- **Switched-off endpoints count toward the allowance:** `createWebhook` in `services/webhook-service.ts` now uses `countEndpoints`, which counts every endpoint. Previously it counted only enabled ones.",
